# S115 (2026-09-05): observability/schemas.json is GENERATED by `schema_registry.py --write` (LF) and
# `--check` compares it BYTE-EXACT. With core.autocrlf=true (this machine) a fresh checkout rewrote the
# committed LF blob as CRLF and `--check` read "registry drift" on an untouched tree — both S115 build
# lanes hit it in fresh worktrees and had to run --write before they could start. No conversion, ever.
observability/schemas.json -text
# S117 (2026-09-06): the same hazard, the other direction. docs/contracts/*.json are BYTE-EXACT
# fixtures (visual_witness_capture_selftest binds packet + schema identity by size/hash) and their
# committed blobs are CRLF. A fresh worktree checkout under core.autocrlf=true added a second CR per
# line (110,341 -> 111,213 bytes = one byte per line) and 6 of 54 tests read GROUND-DRIFT while the
# main checkout — byte-identical to the blob — passed 54/54 (the J39 builder found it, its refuter
# reproduced it). Any file whose bytes ARE the contract must never be converted, in either direction.
docs/contracts/*.json -text
